            { text: "in the ratio of {H} to {L}, and that of {K} to {M}.",
              visible: LMv,
              highlighted: ["E","F","G","H","L","K","M"] },
            { text: "Now, since {E}, {F}, and {G} are the least of the numbers which have the same ratio with {A}, {C}, and {D},",
              visible: LMv,
              highlighted: ["E","F","G","A","C","D"] },
            { text: "and the multitude of the numbers {E}, {F}, and {G} equals the multitude of the numbers {A}, {C}, and {D},",
              visible: LMv,
              highlighted: ["E","F","G","A","C","D"] },
            { text: "therefore, ex aequali {E} is to {G} as {A} is to {D}.",
              visible: LMv,
              highlighted: ["E","G","A","D"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "ex aequali, E : G = A : D", ref: "VII.14" }] },
            { text: "But {E} and {G} are relatively prime, primes are also least,",
              visible: LMv,
              highlighted: ["E","G"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "relatively prime numbers are least", ref: "VII.21" }] },
            { text: "and the least measure those which have the same ratio with them the same number of times,",
              visible: LMv,
              highlighted: ["E","G","A","D"] },
            { text: "the greater the greater and the less the less, that is, the antecedent the antecedent and the consequent the consequent,",
              visible: LMv,
              highlighted: ["E","G","A","D"] },
            { text: "therefore {E} measures {A} the same number of times that {G} measures {D}.",
              visible: LMv,
              highlighted: ["E","A","G","D"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "E measures A as often as G measures D", ref: "VII.20" }] },
            { text: "Let there be as many units in {N} as times that {E} measures {A}.",
              visible: Nv,
              highlighted: ["N","E","A"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "N", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect } ] } },
            { text: "Then {N} multiplied by {E} makes {A}.",
              visible: Nv,
              highlighted: ["N","E","A"] },
            { text: "But {E} is the product of {H} and {K},",
              visible: Nv,
              highlighted: ["E","H","K"] },
            { text: "therefore {N} multiplied by the product of {H} and {K} makes {A}.",
              visible: Nv,
              highlighted: ["N","H","K","A"] },
            { text: "Therefore {A} is solid, and {H}, {K}, and {N} are its sides.",
              visible: Nv,
              highlighted: ["A","H","K","N"] },
            { text: "Again, since {E}, {F}, and {G} are the least of the numbers which have the same ratio as {C}, {D}, and {B},",
              visible: Nv,
              highlighted: ["E","F","G","C","D","B"] },
            { text: "therefore {E} measures {C} the same number of times that {G} measures {B}.",
              visible: Nv,
              highlighted: ["E","C","G","B"] },
            { text: "Let there be as many units in {O} as times that {E} measures {C}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["O","E","C"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "O", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect } ] } },
            { text: "Then {G} measures {B} according to the units in {O}, therefore {O} multiplied by {G} makes {B}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["G","B","O"] },
            { text: "But {G} is the product of {L} and {M},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["G","L","M"] },
            { text: "therefore {O} multiplied by the product of {L} and {M} makes {B}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["O","L","M","B"] },
            { text: "Therefore {B} is solid, and {L}, {M}, and {O} are its sides.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["B","L","M","O"] },
            { text: "Therefore {A} and {B} are solid.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["A","B"] },
            { text: "I say that they are also similar.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["A","B"] },
            { text: "Since {N} and {O} multiplied by {E} make {A} and {C},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["N","O","E","A","C"] },
            { text: "therefore {N} is to {O} as {A} is to {C}, that is, {E} to {F}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["N","O","A","C","E","F"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "N : O = A : C", ref: "VII.18" }] },
            { text: "But {E} is to {F} as {H} is to {L}, and as {K} is to {M},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["E","F","H","L","K","M"] },
            { text: "therefore {H} is to {L} as {K} is to {M}, and as {N} is to {O}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["H","L","K","M","N","O"] },
            { text: "And {H}, {K}, and {N} are the sides of {A}, and {O}, {L}, and {M} the sides of {B}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["H","K","N","A","O","L","M","B"] },
            { text: "Therefore {A} and {B} are similar solid numbers.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["A","B"] },
            { text: "Therefore, if two mean proportional numbers fall between two numbers, then the numbers are similar solid numbers.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["A","C","D","B"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "Q.E.D." }] }
        ],
        resolveJustification: function(ref) {
            if (ref === "VIII.21") return "#prop";
            return (window.eucrefs && window.eucrefs[ref]) || null;
        }
    });

    // Per-page citation lookup for the slideshow's resolveJustification.
    window.eucrefs = (window.eucrefs || {});
    Object.assign(window.eucrefs, {
        "VII.14": "/elements/books/bookVII/propositions/propVII14/",
        "VII.18": "/elements/books/bookVII/propositions/propVII18/",
        "VII.20": "/elements/books/bookVII/propositions/propVII20/",
